# What the Vercel CLI must NOT upload.
#
# The CLI uploads the working tree, so anything git-ignored still rides along
# unless it is named here. `data/sources/` alone holds 140 MB of cached upstream
# archives (the 67 MB barangay GeoJSON, the 24 MB DPWH Parquet, NOAH zips) that
# only the ETL needs — they are never read by a build, and uploading them turns
# every deploy into a multi-minute transfer. `apps/web/.next` and `node_modules`
# are rebuilt by the platform.
#
# Keep this file next to the repo root because the deployment is rooted at the
# repo root (the project's Root Directory is `apps/web` and its install/build
# commands `cd ../..`), so the workspace — and this file — must be in the snapshot.

# Cached upstream downloads and partial transfers (ETL-only)
data/sources
**/*.part

# ETL scratch: cached archive captures, probe scripts, run logs
tools/etl/.cache

# Local environment files. NEVER upload these — the deployment gets its values
# from Vercel project settings, and `.env.local` holds a real database URI.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The platform builds these itself
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
**/dist
.vercel

# Local toolchain noise
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
